---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import EmailCapture from '../components/EmailCapture.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Never Again: The DJ USB Prevention System | Save My Gig!"
  description="The exact system that makes USB failures a non-event: redundant drives, clean exports, proper ejects, and the gear that doesn't die."
  path="/prepare"
>
  <main class="wrap">
    <div class="status-line">Prevention_Hub</div>

    <h1 style="margin-bottom:1rem">NEVER <span class="accent">AGAIN</span></h1>
    <p class="dim" style="margin-bottom:2rem">USB failures aren't bad luck. They're a missing system. This is the system.</p>

    <div class="panel">
      <!-- "The seven rules" until 2026-07-27. Antonio: no count in the name,
           because it could be seven today, eight tomorrow, twelve after that,
           and then we fix copy sitewide forever. The lint now enforces it. -->
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:0.75rem">The mandatory rules</h3>
      <ol class="rules-ol">
        <li><strong>Two identical USBs, every gig.</strong> Same export on both. One in the bag, one in your pocket.</li>
        <li><strong>FAT32, always.</strong> NTFS never works. exFAT is a gamble in a booth you do not control, since only newer players read it. Pick <span class="mono">MBR</span> when the format tool offers you a scheme.</li>
        <li><strong>Quality drives only.</strong> The $8 no-name stick is how this story starts. <a href="/gear">Approved drives →</a></li>
        <li><strong>Eject properly, every time.</strong> From Rekordbox and from the player (<span class="mono">USB STOP</span>).</li>
        <li><strong>Re-export after every library change.</strong> An old export is a corrupt export waiting to happen.</li>
        <li><strong>Test on a player</strong> (or at least re-open in Rekordbox) before leaving home.</li>
        <li><strong>Back up the Rekordbox library</strong> monthly to a different drive or cloud.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <!-- Antonio's rule, kept OUTSIDE the numbered list. The old reason was
         protecting the homepage's "seven rules" count; that count is gone now,
         but the separation still earns its place: this one is about TIME, not
         gear, so it reads as its own law rather than one more list item. -->
    <div class="alert-card" style="margin-top:1rem">
      <div style="font-size:20px" aria-hidden="true">🔒</div>
      <div>
        <strong>And the rule about time: gig day is a freeze.</strong> No
        rekordbox update, no firmware update, no OS update on the day you play,
        or close to it. A fresh version can bring a fresh problem, and the booth
        is where you will meet it. Manufacturers have pulled player firmware
        after it emptied DJs' browse screens mid-set. Update the week after a
        gig, never the day before one.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="panel panel-go">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:0.6rem">Before you leave: the checklist</h3>
      <p class="dim" style="margin-bottom:1rem">Tick off the basics, the technical gear, and the life stuff you forget on the way out. It tracks your readiness and saves on this device for next time.</p>
      <a href="/checklist" class="btn btn-go" data-event="checklist_open" data-placement="prepare">Open the pre-gig checklist</a>
    </div>

    <EmailCapture
      source="prepare"
      title="The Emergency Card"
      blurb="One page. Everything to check before you leave, and the first moves when a player refuses your drive. Read it free any time, or get the printable version emailed so it lives on your phone."
    />

    <div class="grid section">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>🔌 The gear that doesn't die</h3>
        <p>The exact drives worth carrying, and why.</p>
        <a href="/gear" class="btn btn-neutral" data-event="affiliate_click" data-program="gear_page" data-placement="prepare">See the kit</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  /* The homepage door promises "the mandatory rules" with no count on
     purpose; the numbers HERE are fine, a list may show its own length. */
  .rules-ol { list-style: none; counter-reset: rl; margin: 1.2rem 0 0; padding: 0; }
  .rules-ol li {
    counter-increment: rl;
    position: relative;
    padding: 0.75rem 0 0.75rem 2.2rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--edge-soft);
  }
  .rules-ol li:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .rules-ol li::before {
    content: counter(rl);
    position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0.75rem;
    width: 1.5rem; text-align: center;
    font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 800; color: var(--red);
  }
</style>
